Z||000000||AkursedX||08-04-2000||12:54 AM||||Ok, well me and my dad we're having a conversation at the dinner table about modding my car (we do this alot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )  He's an experienced mechanic of 30 years so I feel confident he knows what he's talking about.<P>Anyways...<BR>I was discussing with my father about my exhaust system project (Sprint Manifolds from the Fiero store, removing the Cat, and that Borla Exhaust system from Fieroparts) i figure to do it by October.  Well he brought up the point of a big loss of back pressure due to the mods and that it wouldn't idle properly, or else idle at very high rpm's.<BR>I was wondering if anyone who has this type of setup has encountered any sort of problems like I mentioned.  I told him that the Idle Air Control Valve controlled the idle, and that it would be ok.  Just curious to see if anyone else has any problems.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>btw I have an 88 GT v-6||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-04-2000||02:08 AM||||Hmmmmm..Ive never heard that before. My Fieros are all stock, but, my Formula dosnt have a cat, and it idles perfectly. (Im going to put a new cat. on it, its too loud and sounds like a redneck car!)...<BR>Im not very familiar with using the Sprint headers, or if that would cause a prob. I dont really see it causing any probs, but I may be wrong....anybody else? Ogre? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||08-04-2000||02:25 AM||||Yeah, I don't forsee any problems either, I think it's more my father thinking of the worst possible scenario.  <BR>I am worried about the noise though.  I had a big hole in my cat a few months ago and it sounded awful, I'm hoping it won't be as bad done properly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||02-25-1996||12:49 AM||||I had a set of Chris Wests (flo-well) headers, no cat and 2.5" exhaust. the exhaust sounded sweet. i took the cat off and lost 4lbft of torque.. i then got the headers and lost even MORE torque... bjust porting the factory manifolds is the best HP for the money. unless you have a turbo, S/C, nitrous or a bigger motor than the 2.8. I can post the dyno results if you'd like. it ides fine, hauls butt. GT Bastard now has the car. you'll be fine in the idle department.. just lacking on the torque if you get headers. The decrease in back pressure is what caused the slump in torque.  ||||reg||1
